{
  "version": 1,
  "about": "Technology area (domain) of a repository (SPEC addendum H). Rules are tried top to bottom and the FIRST match wins; a repo that matches none is 'other'. Each rule matches ONE field: topics (GitHub topics, exact; 'kube*' matches topics starting with kube), name (the repo name and the owner login split into words on punctuation and camelCase: a keyword must equal a word or 2-3 consecutive words written together, so 'freecodecamp' matches freeCodeCamp but 'unity' does not match community; 'kube*' matches words starting with kube; 'json-schema' matches those words in that order), description (whole words or phrases of the repo description, 'vulnerabilit*' matches word starts) or languages (GitHub primary language, then the largest language by bytes; '(none)' = GitHub detected no language). The phases are ordered topics > name > description > language, so maintainers' own labels win over guesses from the language. Repos without topics (all of them until the repo metadata refresh has run) fall through to the name, description and language rules.",
